-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Gryzor
  Publisher   Ocean, 1987
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Gryzor (1987)(Ocean)(48K-128K).z80
  MD5         fdab5fb61b2cb01ce38edcfa85ea9e80

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same file;
              probe 0xA439 (the player's controls read, once per game update);
              input keyed to updates; both runs in lockstep at every update in
              all 15 trials)

  Changes     1.0: figures and bullets as Next sprites; black outline;
              Sinclair's 48K ROM as the alt ROM; hooks at 28 MHz restoring the
              game's speed; R kept, so the game's random numbers are the
              original's; the original's pace kept by a pace limiter and
              prepared sprite patterns
              1.1: rebuilt on NexClash's shared pace code; plays at the
              original's pace as 1.0 did

  Note        Keys: hold 0 on the menu to start (the menu checks the keyboard
              every few frames); cursor keys 5 left, 8 right, 7 jump, 6 down,
              0 fire. The player, enemies and bullets are Next sprites with a
              black outline (the owner's choice), so they show one colour
              across the jungle's bands; scenery, stars, objects and text keep
              the original's colours. Plays at the original's pace (hooks at
              28 MHz, your speed restored) and gives the same enemies for the
              same keys. 1.1, 5 trials a scene: quiet +0.00%, busy +0.64%
              (worst +1.52%), firing +0.48%. Known issues: in the yellow
              forest the black outline meets the forest's black pattern, so
              figures read less well there; while the scenery scrolls, a
              figure can show a frame behind it now and then. Missing: this is
              the 48K form, so the first section only and no 128K music; no
              Enhanced colour set (a trial set was shelved); the cheats are
              the archive's, checked on a simulator only; not yet checked:
              Kempston and define keys; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immune to enemies touch
   3  Immune to enemy fire

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

